You can make it. Chances are, you left lots of useful stuff
in the dungeon. But you need to be as efficient as possible
in gathering up what you need because the longer you take,
the more stuff will be cursed.

Food. You can probably live off the land easily enough until
you leave Gehennom and then pick up a dozen K rations in the
castle.

Boots, if there are no more speed boots, jumping boots would
be a good second choice. You can Elbereth a hole in the
crowd and then jump 2 or three spaces. Levitation boots
might be too dangerous, if they got cursed with your god mad
and no HW or ?oRC you could never pick anything up for the
rest of the game. Fountains, nymphs or incubi might not be
found quickly enough. At least with the ring you might get
it blasted off. If you put on the =oSearch and it gets
cursed you may not be able to navigate the plane of air.

Does the absence of a towel and blindfold indicate no
telepathy? That would be a good thing for finding a few
nymphs on the way out to get some potions. That would be
useful if you plan to stop for a sac session.

Where is your luckstone? Where is your lizard corpse? What a
sorry collection of rings. You may need a pick axe on the
plane of earth. The /oLightning would be best used for
Elbereth when Rodney summons pets.

You need a sack so you can keep that =oLev from getting
cursed. Even a large box might do in a pinch. I don't know
if carrying other items, like 20 uniquely named gems,
reduces the chances of a particular item being cursed.

It would be worth the time to get back in your god's good
graces if you left behind some c?oCM or /oCM. If you need
some time on a level you can protect the "oYendor by leaving
it on the upstairs of the next lower level. BTW, name it
right now!

Your Orb of Fate should find two portals for you, I'd use it
on air and fire. If you left behind any ?oGD or /oSDD they
would be useful in finding the other portals.

With only a unihorn (you might pick up a spare on the way
out) to cure me, I'd fear Pestilence the most and reserve
the /oDeath for him. You need to be able to move quickly and
sometimes you can't avoid stopping to kill something. Two
weaponing with a long sword would speed things up. I usually
find a few blessed long swords during a game an a high
percentage of the blessed long swords are enchanted.

In short, I'd rather go quickly with minimal additions to my
meager kit than take 20,000 turn in hopes I could
substantially improve it. Small delays for specific
improvements are worth it.

